---
/*
  The Technology Blueprint's ground: its sub-brand, one graphic wherever
  the service shows (the nav's Services card, the homepage deck's card,
  the service page's hero). The AEC Tech Partners hero's lattice
  (Hero.astro, .hero__lattice): a draughtsman's dash-dot line, a dot on
  every crossing (mountIsoField, dot-field.js, data-iso-line="dash"), but
  at the site's drawings' 30° rather than that hero's flatter 2:1, a
  cell of that hero's size (8.5rem).
  It fills its parent (styles.css, "Service grounds"), behind
  everything in it, set out from its middle and cropped by its edges.

  module: the cell, in the screen's units (or in the units of the
  sibling svg the field takes its scale from: the nav's card, whose
  pattern box is 400 wide).
  on: a drawing in the ground's parent (a selector: the service page
  hero's diagram) the ground is set out from instead, through its
  origin (data-ground) at its scale, a whole number of its cells (54)
  to the ground's, as near the screen's 136 as that allows
  (dot-field.js, data-iso-cell): the drawing stands on the ground, its
  slab's edges and its setting-out on the ground's lines.
*/
interface Props {
  module?: number;
  on?: string;
  class?: string;
}
const { module = 136, on, class: className } = Astro.props;
---
<div class:list={["service-ground", "blueprint-ground", className]} data-iso-field data-iso-line="dash" data-iso-module={on ? 54 : module} data-iso-ground={on} data-iso-cell={on ? 136 : undefined} aria-hidden="true"></div>
